OL,3,GNEWSAMinister looking again at patient
OL,4,Atravel costs to UK
OL,5,
OL,6,FJersey's health minister says he will
OL,7,Fconsider whether "UK travel should
OL,8,Fcontinue to be paid for all patients in
OL,9,Fall circumstances".
OL,11,FSenator Tom Binet was responding to a
OL,12,Fcall from the Jersey Health Advisory
OL,13,FBoard to see if travel costs could be
OL,14,Fcut.
OL,16,FCarolyn Downs, a non-executive director
OL,17,Fof the board described current
OL,18,Fprovision as "very generous".
OL,23,APub: 02-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
